#N canvas 40 40 760 560 12;
#X text 20 15 multipink~ - four calibrated pink-noise streams (seam-ltm);
#X text 20 45 No inlet \, no arguments \, no controls. Four independent pink streams - the reference for calibrating the stone band by band. Every third-octave band is at -39.5 dBFS at any sample rate. The total RMS is the sum of the bands up to fs/2 \, so it moves with the rate: -23.0 dBFS at 48 kHz (hence the name -23) \, about +0.28 dB per doubling (-22.7 at 96 kHz). Same DSP as the seam-ltm VST3 MULTIPINK: these are the streams of a 4-channel instance on pool slots 1-4 at Reference -23 Trim 0 \, sample for sample. The streams restart from their seeds whenever DSP is switched on., f 95;
#X obj 20 170 multipink~;
#X obj 420 170 tgl 19 0 empty empty listen on dac~ 1-4 24 10 0 12 #dfdfdf #000000 #000000 0 1;
#X obj 20 220 env~ 4096;
#X obj 20 250 - 100;
#X obj 20 280 vu 15 120 empty ch1 -1 -10 0 12 #404040 #000000 1 0;
#X obj 20 440 *~ 0;
#X obj 120 220 env~ 4096;
#X obj 120 250 - 100;
#X obj 120 280 vu 15 120 empty ch2 -1 -10 0 12 #404040 #000000 1 0;
#X obj 120 440 *~ 0;
#X obj 220 220 env~ 4096;
#X obj 220 250 - 100;
